module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.tail_call_match_lowering_skips_rc_arm_grouping

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data tail_call_match_lowering_skips_rc_arm_grouping: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "tail_call_match_lowering_skips_rc_arm_grouping" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: an exhaustive .dag match whose arms discriminate a variant nested under an Rc-shared field (`TypeNode { connective: Conj }` beside `TypeNode { connective: Disj }` ...) inside a function whose self-call is lowered to a loop. The front end accepts it with zero diagnostics; the emitted Rust refuses with E0004 (`pattern NodeKind::TypeNode { .. } not covered`).",

    "MECHANISM: the ordinary match renderer groups arms that share an outer variant into one nested match on the Rc field (v1.compiler.emit_rust rc_grouped_arm_plan, the #8570 grouping), so an enumerated nested arm set stays visible to rustc's exhaustiveness check. The tail-call renderer (emit_rust_tco_match / emit_typed_tco_match_arm) never consults that grouping: every nested discrimination is emitted as a match GUARD (collect_pattern_rc_variant_guards), and rustc does not count guarded arms toward exhaustiveness. No arm is dropped and none is selected wrongly -- the arms are all present, guarded -- so the failure is loud at the target compiler, an instance of accepted_source_emits_uncompilable_target specific to the loop path.",

    "WHY IT WAS DORMANT: every such match on main ended in a `_ =>` wildcard, which gave rustc an unguarded arm to close over. The typed NFR burn-down (gunbc#12610 census) replaced those wildcards with enumerated variants, and the first enumerated nested arm set inside a tail-recursive walk surfaced it: v2.compiler.target_serialize grammar_tokens_fold_list_targets_into, emit-build of the 00_compile closure on gunbc#12667.",

    "INTERIM FORM, and its dissolution condition: that walk now matches a flat two-variant step returned by a non-recursive helper (v2.compiler.target_serialize grammar_tokens_fold_list_shape), which the NFR ruling prescribes for self-calling functions (delegate the decision, keep the self-call). The helper stays correct once the lowering is fixed; what dissolves is the NEED for it -- when emit_rust_tco_match renders nested arm sets through the same grouping as the ordinary renderer, a tail-recursive function may match nested variants directly and the step may be folded back.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1 at best (the target compiler refuses; gunbc accepts). CEILING: 3 -- the emitter can decide exhaustiveness on the same facts for both renderers. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the tail-call match renderer consumes rc_grouped_arm_plan (one grouping authority for both match lowerings), proven by an enumerated nested arm set in a tail-recursive fixture that emits and builds.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.emit_rust", decl_name: "emit_rust_tco_match"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.emit_rust", decl_name: "rc_grouped_arm_plan"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v2.compiler.target_serialize", decl_name: "grammar_tokens_fold_list_shape"),
  ],
}
